<title>NETHERLANDS: SPORT7 GAINS FOUR PCT OF DUTCH TV AUDIENCE IN SEPT.</title>
<headline>SPORT7 GAINS FOUR PCT OF DUTCH TV AUDIENCE IN SEPT.</headline>
<dateline>HILVERSUM, Netherlands 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new Sport7</p>
<p>channel gained a four percent share of the Dutch television</p>
<p>audience in September, its first full month of operation.</p>
<p>The NOS audience research unit published the following Dutch</p>
<p>television viewing figures for September:</p>
<p>    Channel     Audience share in pct:  Sept 96  Aug 96  Sept 96</p>
<p>    RTL4					    21	 18	 23</p>
<p>    NL1					     14	 15	 12</p>
<p>    NL2					     13	 13	 15</p>
<p>    NL3					     10	 11	 12</p>
<p>    Veronica					 8	  7	 11</p>
<p>    SBS6					     7	  8	  3</p>
<p>    RTL5					     6	  6	  6</p>
<p>    Sport7					   4	  3	  0</p>
<p>    Arcade					   2	  2	  1</p>
<p>    Other channels				15	 17	 17</p>
<p>NOTES - NL1, NL2 and NL3 are public channels. RTL4, RTL5,</p>
<p>Veronica, SBS and Sport7 are commercial channels. Arcade figures</p>
<p>are combined total for its TV10 and Music Factory channels.</p>
<p>OWNERSHIP DETAILS:</p>
<p>RTL4 and RTL5 -- Dutch publisher VNU owns 38 pct</p>
<p>of both channels, Luxembourg-based CLT owns 61 pct of both.</p>
<p>SBS6 -- Scandinavian Broadcasting System owns 70</p>
<p>pct of SBS6, Dutch publisher De Telegraaf 30 percent.</p>
<p>TV10 and Music Factory -- Both channels are wholly owned</p>
<p>units of Dutch media group Wegener Arcade .</p>
<p>Sport7 -- PTT Nederland , ING , Philips</p>
<p>Electronics and Dutch TV production firm Endemol each</p>
<p>own 19.5 percent stakes in Sport7. Dutch soccer association KNVB</p>
<p>has a 10 percent stake and De Telegraaf five percent.</p>
<p>Veronica -- Left the public broadcasting system in 1995 to</p>
<p>become a commercial station.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
